<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>NYT Business Full-Text Feed</title><link>file:///Users/purp/Downloads/translator/xml/Business_fulltext.xml</link><description>Full-text NYT Business articles</description><atom:link href="file:///Users/purp/Downloads/translator/xml/Business_fulltext.xml" rel="self"/><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 22:30:45 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>These Countries Embrace E.V.s to Avoid Oil Price Shocks</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/03/business/electric-vehicles-costa-rica.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/04/29/multimedia/00biz-iran-ev-boom-vid-wthb/00biz-iran-ev-boom-vid-wthb-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg"/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
People in Costa Rica and other Latin American, Asian and African countries are increasingly buying electric vehicles to avoid spiking fuel prices.
]]&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/03/business/electric-vehicles-costa-rica.html</guid><pubDate>Sun, 03 May 2026 00:00:36 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Driving Electric in Costa Rica Is Surprisingly Doable</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/03/business/costa-rica-electric-vehicle-road-trip.html</link><description>&lt;![CDATA[
